  "instance_name": "musical_beat_metaphor",
  "label": "Metaphor: 'Beat' as Aggression",
  "description": "The phrase 'they always love a good beat' uses the concept of a musical 'beat' to imply physical rhythm or aggression, which is a culturally loaded metaphor. In this context, it is used to stereotype Black people as inherently linked to violence or physicality, despite music being a rich and diverse cultural expression.",
